 1  B
 CH2 + photon = CH + H
!
! photoabsorption cross section and photodissociation yield from Leiden database (Heays et al 2017, A&A, 602, A105, https://home.strw.leidenuniv.nl/~ewine/photo/)
!
! there are two photodissociation channels (CH + H) and (C + H2) but the latter is a minor one (Kroes et al 1997, J Chem Phys, 107, 5757)
!
! photoionization threshold is 119 nm (no data on photoionization cross section except the relative data in the ionization threshold region by Litorja & Ruscic 1998, J Chem Phys, 108, 6748)
!
! sigma is the total photoabsorption cross section
! yield is the photodissociation yield relative to photoabsorption, which in this case is 1 everywhere
!
! wlth[nm]  sigma[cm2]   yield(s)...
